WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.210
38th
Karai Summer
Extravaganza
8/20,
4:00PM

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.170
Nanako-chan, Eiji-kun! Sorry I made you wait.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.170
Nah, it's no big deal.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.500
Wow... Look at you, Nanako-chan!

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.250
I had a feeling you'd look great in a yukata!

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.040
You don't look so bad either, Eiji-

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.290
How'd you already catch all those?!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.000
He got here
two hours early.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.500
Gentle words

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.630
Soft feelings

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.540
Precious memories

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.100
They're dyed with love

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:51.330
When I'm with you, even getting caught
in the rain turns into something new

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.540
What words can I string together

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.710
To keep this color from fading away?

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.250
I know

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:05.210
What the two of us will 
become on that far-off day

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.630
Isn't that right, God?

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.130
Waiting for the train, the 
water droplets beading up

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.710
I really wish this moment

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.710
Could somehow last forever

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.750
Is that too much to ask?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:31.980
Poem 11
Watching the Fireworks with You

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.250
You're certainly in a good mood, Nanako-chan.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.190
I'm looking forward

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.490
To watching the fireworks

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:43.630
With Ei-chan tonight!

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.360
I'm so excited!

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.690
I was up almost all night

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:53.880
Thinking about it.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.840
Oh man, are you serious? 
You're such a little kid.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.650
Wait, so does that mean

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.990
You actually managed to

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.280
Fall asleep last night?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.880
Sure did. In fact, I slept like a log!

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.350
Why's that?

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.420
I was out bug-catchin' 
the whole day yesterday.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.380
What are you, five?!
Why are you so obsessed with bugs?!

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.090
Oh God, I'm a third wheel!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.000
What's the matter, President?!

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.930
Huh? Ooh!

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.640
WIN PRIZES!            Raffle Booth
Draw Here

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:41.880
A raffle, huh?

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.850
Grand Prize

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.630
Whoa!

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.130
They've got some cool stuff! Let's go!

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.460
5th prize, eh?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.500
Aw! I wanted that FamiStation!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.420
Congratulations! Here's your glow ring.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.960
Damn, that thing's bright!

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.950
Oh my gosh, how cute!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.260
I think it's an awesome prize.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.350
You hit the jackpot.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.920
You think so? Well, I guess 
if you like it so much...

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:21.250
Whoa, jeez... Is it really THAT exciting?

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.290
W-we have ourselves a grand prize winner!

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.080
Enjoy.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.960
I'd be a lot happier if you 
gave me a boyfriend instead...

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.080
I can't wait for the fireworks!

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.170
Same here.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.580
I might be statin' the obvious,
but there's a lotta couples here...

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.960
Of course! Going on a date
at a festival is super romantic!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.180
Back when they were young,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.570
My papa asked my mom out

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.020
At a festival.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.710
No way, that's so cute! How'd he do it?

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.990
Well, he turned to her

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.600
And placed a small peony

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.090
Gently in her hand...

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:10.850
Oh wow, a peony! That's pretty smooth!

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.920
Why'd he do that?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.460
Peonies usually symbolize shyness.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.130
They evoke a very sweet and 
soft image of femininity.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.130
Sweet and soft...?

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.460
Whatever you're imagining right 
now, it's probably wrong.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.710
Not only that, peonies are often used
as a metaphor for a beautiful woman.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.130
"She stands as a garden peony,

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.290
Sits as a tree peony,

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.790
And walks as a lily."

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.130
Haven't you heard that one?

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.080
Is this lady some kinda
crazy, shape-shifting plant monster?!

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.550
Alright. Next club meeting, we're having
a SERIOUS literature lesson.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.960
Huh? Uh, okay.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.920
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.670
Oh, me too!

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.630
Huh? You wanna go pee together, President?

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.130
I'm not going IN with you!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.880
Nanako-chan!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.000
Your yukata is so cute!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.960
Nanako, the fireworks are about to start!

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.720
We saved the perfect spot,
so you should come watch them with us.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.630
C'mon, let's go!

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.370
B-but I wanted to...

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:41.290
Watch them alone with Ei-chan...

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.630
Just the two of us...

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.070
Aw crap...

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.670
There're too many people behind me...
I'm gettin' stage fright...

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.420
Sorry I took so long!

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:54.670
Huh?

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.050
Apparently Nanako got pulled 
away by a bunch of girls

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.330
from her class to go watch the fireworks...

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.290
She's really gotta learn 
how to say no sometimes...

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:06.460
At least she didn't get lost or anything.
There's no need to panic...

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:08.950
I'm looking forward

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.300
To watching the fireworks

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.660
With Ei-chan tonight!

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.420
Okay, maybe we oughta panic a little...

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:19.710
They've got to be around 
here somewhere, but...

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.110
it's gonna be tough to spot 
her in a crowd this big.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.580
I have a plan!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.510
But first...

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.400
I gotta go finish my pee break.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.830
Why didn't you finish it earlier?!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.290
Oh, Nanako-chan!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.920
Are you here by yourself?

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.840
I'm sorry, you guys...

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.410
I didn't come here alone.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:46.380
I came with someone.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.290
What? Really?

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.380
Oh my gosh, did you come with a date?!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.850
Where'd all those tanzaku come from...?

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:00.690
Hey...!

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.460
Eiji-kun, I can't run that fast...!

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.310
It's starting! I gotta hurry!

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.920
W-wait...!

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.080
So pretty...

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.830
How am I s'posed to find her 
in the middle of all this?!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.630
Is something wrong?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.710
'Scuse me! Pardon me!

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.000
Rude...

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.660
Comin' through!

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.060
All I really want

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.480
Is to watch the fireworks

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.100
With Ei-chan tonight...

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.080
Eiji-kun...

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.170
I really hope you make it in time...

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.080
A FamiStation!

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.710
Hanabi-chan?!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.040
Good evening, Miss President!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.750
Good evening!

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.950
Hiya.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.290
Where're Eiji and Nanako-chan?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.580
Well, we kinda got separated...

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.540
They changed colors!

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.790
Some of them are a different shape
than they were a minute ago...

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:02.710
Those ones are a different type altogether.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.460
Huh...?

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.250
Fireworks that fan out

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.980
and leave trails of sparks
in the sky have a "chrysanthemum" effect.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.610
Then what about the ones without trails?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.670
If it leaves a trail, 
it's a "chrysanthemum"...

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.080
If it doesn't...

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:29.870
...it's a "peony."

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.710
I found you!

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:46.600
I swear... Didn't you say we were gonna
watch the fireworks together?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.000
I wouldn't have found you 
if it weren't for that ring.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:54.380
You're just about the only person
who'd actually wear somethin' so lame.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.210
Huh?!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:03.250
Nanako-chan, are you and 
Busujima-kun going out?!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.670
Wha-?! N-no!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:11.290
I just promised her we'd watch
the fireworks together! That's all!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.290
That sounds an awful lot like
something a couple would do!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.380
Wh-whatever...

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:08.600
It's almost funny how different we are

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:14.000
Down to our reflections in the shop window

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:19.670
When you smile as brightly as the sun

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:28.210
A peaceful feeling washes over me

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:35.420
Even my trivial, everyday life

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:41.000
Begins to shine when I'm with you

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.460
Even if something happened

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:47.630
Even if we hurt each other sometimes

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:54.960
Believe in our ordinary days

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.190
On the next epi-

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.650
-sode of Senryu Girl:

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:02.960
Nanako and Ei-

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:03.900
-ji!

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:07.040
Next Time, Poem 12
"Nanako and Eiji"
